dcomp, winewayland.drv: show CEP panels hosted in a plain app window (Audition Learn panel)

Audition 2026's Learn panel stayed white while DevTools showed the page fully rendered
(Neutron discussion #8). Two gaps on the CEP panel present path:

* dcomp found the panel host only by PlugPlug class name (WC_PLUGPLUG_HTMLEXTENSION in
  Premiere, PLUGPLUG_UI_NATIVE in Animate). Audition hosts CEP panels in its own DVA
  window (Chrome_WidgetWin_0 <- CefBrowserWindow <- {guid} <- DroverLord ...), so no host
  was found and the frames were registered against CEF's own window, where nothing draws
  them. Add a structural fallback with the shape all three apps share: the host is the
  window directly above the {guid} container, which is CefBrowserWindow's parent in the
  app's process. Used only when neither class matches.

* winewayland's consumer drew through GetDC(host), which honors WS_CLIPCHILDREN. Audition's
  host has it, and its {guid} child covers it completely, so every blit was clipped to
  nothing. Draw without clipping children (they are the panel these pixels belong to);
  siblings are still honored.

--- a/dlls/dcomp/device.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/device.c
@@ -205,7 +205,7 @@
     HWND a;
     int depth;
 
-    HWND native_host = NULL;
+    HWND native_host = NULL, container_host = NULL;
 
     /* NEUTRON 2026-08-04: Adobe uses TWO different CEP host window classes, and matching only the
      * first one meant a whole app never got this present path:
@@ -221,7 +221,17 @@
      * ⚠️ Deliberately ADDITIVE: HTMLEXTENSION still wins outright, and the native host is only used
      * when the chain contains no HTMLEXTENSION at all. Returning whichever matched FIRST while
      * walking up would have changed which ancestor Premiere selects, and Premiere's panel works
-     * today -- this must not disturb it. */
+     * today -- this must not disturb it.
+     *
+     * NEUTRON 2026-10-12: a THIRD host, with no PlugPlug class at all. Audition 2026 hosts its CEP
+     * panels in its own DVA windows: Chrome_WidgetWin_0 <- CefBrowserWindow <- {guid} <-
+     * DroverLord - Window Class <- ... (Neutron discussion #8: the Audition Learn panel stayed
+     * WHITE while DevTools showed the page fully rendered). What all three apps share is the
+     * SHAPE: the {guid} container is CefBrowserWindow's parent, lives in the Adobe app's process,
+     * and the host is the window directly above it -- HTMLEXTENSION in Premiere,
+     * PLUGPLUG_UI_NATIVE in Animate, a DroverLord in Audition (measured: the same 505x346 rect as
+     * the panel content; the DroverLord above that adds the tab header). Used only when neither
+     * class matched, so Premiere and Animate select exactly what they did before. */
     for (a = hwnd, depth = 0; a && depth < 16; a = GetAncestor(a, GA_PARENT), depth++)
     {
         if (GetClassNameW(a, cls, 128) <= 0) continue;
@@ -229,8 +239,19 @@
             return a;
         if (!native_host && wcsstr(cls, L"PLUGPLUG_UI_NATIVE"))
             native_host = a;
+        if (!container_host && !wcscmp(cls, L"CefBrowserWindow"))
+        {
+            HWND container = GetAncestor(a, GA_PARENT), above;
+            DWORD cef_pid = 0, container_pid = 0;
+
+            GetWindowThreadProcessId(a, &cef_pid);
+            if (container && GetWindowThreadProcessId(container, &container_pid)
+                    && container_pid != cef_pid
+                    && (above = GetAncestor(container, GA_PARENT)) && above != GetDesktopWindow())
+                container_host = above;
+        }
     }
-    return native_host;
+    return native_host ? native_host : container_host;
 }
 
 static struct list presentations = LIST_INIT(presentations);
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/dllmain.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/dllmain.c
@@ -168,7 +168,16 @@
     bmi.bmiHeader.biBitCount = 32;
     bmi.bmiHeader.biCompression = BI_RGB;
 
-    if ((hdc = GetDC(hwnd)))
+    /* NEUTRON 2026-10-12: never clip the host's CHILDREN. Those children are the panel itself --
+     * the {guid} container and CEF's windows, which cover the host completely -- and these pixels
+     * are what they would show. GetDC() honors WS_CLIPCHILDREN, so on a host that has it the
+     * visible region was EMPTY and every blit was discarded: Audition 2026 hosts its CEP panels in
+     * a DVA DroverLord window (style 0x52000000) and its Learn panel stayed white while frames were
+     * delivered. Clearing the style on that window by hand made the panel appear at once.
+     * Premiere's and Animate's PlugPlug hosts render through this path today, which they could not
+     * do if they clipped children, so their clipping is unchanged. Siblings are still honored. */
+    if ((hdc = GetDCEx(hwnd, 0, DCX_CACHE |
+                       ((GetWindowLongW(hwnd, GWL_STYLE) & WS_CLIPSIBLINGS) ? DCX_CLIPSIBLINGS : 0))))
     {
         static int (WINAPI *p_SetStretchBltMode)(HDC, int);
         static int (WINAPI *p_StretchDIBits)(HDC, int, int, int, int, int, int, int, int,
